    "stem": "The diagram shows Chirag's and Leela's square dosas of the same whole size. Chirag cuts his into $3$ equal pieces. Leela cuts hers into $3$ pieces of different sizes. Each takes one piece and calls it one-third of the dosa.",
    "item_type": "structured",
    "options": {},
    "statements": [],
    "parts": [
      {
        "id": "i",
        "text": "Which claim correctly decides whose piece is a valid one-third?",
        "marks": 1,
        "options": [
          {
            "id": "A",
            "text": "Only Chirag's piece is one-third, because the whole was split into equal-size parts."
          },
          {
            "id": "B",
            "text": "Both pieces are one-third, because each person took one of three pieces."
          },
          {
            "id": "C",
            "text": "Calling a piece one-third is what forces the dosa cuts to be equal."
          }
        ]
      },
